{"attributes":{"stable_path":"/documentation/Documentation@72790a76-5799-4410-b036-b012d3f5ff59","sysml_id":"72790a76-5799-4410-b036-b012d3f5ff59","element_id":"72790a76-5799-4410-b036-b012d3f5ff59","sysml_type":"Documentation","owner_id":"43885c39-6253-44ee-bfd2-e5e7e82eafc4","owning_namespace_id":"43885c39-6253-44ee-bfd2-e5e7e82eafc4","owning_relationship_id":"75ca1185-a143-475f-a875-4f8de8f8bd43","owning_membership_id":"75ca1185-a143-475f-a875-4f8de8f8bd43","is_library_element":false,"is_implied_included":false,"body":"Combines channel status and environment evidence into current capability. Monitoring continues during startup and degraded mode. Startup/recovery timers belong to the lifecycle controller. TDS_SEN_005, TDS_ODD_001 through TDS_ODD_006. "},"concept":"documentation","metamodel":"SysMLv2","namespace":"System_Model_Tiger_Detection"},
{"attributes":{"stable_path":"/documentation/Documentation@74794d5b-82d2-406b-89f1-fdab2888351a","sysml_id":"74794d5b-82d2-406b-89f1-fdab2888351a","element_id":"74794d5b-82d2-406b-89f1-fdab2888351a","sysml_type":"Documentation","owner_id":"ca8fc8a1-be36-4992-bbd4-a7f3ec9c57c7","owning_namespace_id":"ca8fc8a1-be36-4992-bbd4-a7f3ec9c57c7","owning_relationship_id":"228e5a0b-704a-42e7-b97e-6a2d58b36c2b","owning_membership_id":"228e5a0b-704a-42e7-b97e-6a2d58b36c2b","is_library_element":false,"is_implied_included":false,"body":"Thermal image frame from the infrared sensor. Requirement: TDS_SEN_003. "},"concept":"documentation","metamodel":"SysMLv2","namespace":"System_Model_Tiger_Detection"},
{"attributes":{"stable_path":"/documentation/Documentation@74b2f560-fa72-4e1a-a8bc-bbd192a7e6ab","sysml_id":"74b2f560-fa72-4e1a-a8bc-bbd192a7e6ab","element_id":"74b2f560-fa72-4e1a-a8bc-bbd192a7e6ab","sysml_type":"Documentation","owner_id":"915da102-aaf2-4fca-8f3e-de6744ab7e2c","owning_namespace_id":"915da102-aaf2-4fca-8f3e-de6744ab7e2c","owning_relationship_id":"9aa39038-6049-4207-8510-7ea2709cb648","owning_membership_id":"9aa39038-6049-4207-8510-7ea2709cb648","is_library_element":false,"is_implied_included":false,"body":"WarningsSystem lifecycle: a tiger detection enters alertingChange;\na further detection resets it; a stop command or timeout returns to\nidle. Requirements: TDS_WRN_001, TDS_WRN_004.\n"},"concept":"documentation","metamodel":"SysMLv2","namespace":"System_Model_Tiger_Detection"},
{"attributes":{"stable_path":"/documentation/Documentation@7d05b716-1eda-4c7c-aef6-6076e1884749","sysml_id":"7d05b716-1eda-4c7c-aef6-6076e1884749","element_id":"7d05b716-1eda-4c7c-aef6-6076e1884749","sysml_type":"Documentation","owner_id":"dd93f14e-0b5e-4556-9754-7076efb77a20","owning_namespace_id":"dd93f14e-0b5e-4556-9754-7076efb77a20","owning_relationship_id":"c4d6e0fb-c29a-4549-90bf-e845f2626d04","owning_membership_id":"c4d6e0fb-c29a-4549-90bf-e845f2626d04","is_library_element":false,"is_implied_included":false,"body":"Performs tiger/non-tiger classification AFTER fusion and temporal confirmation, using both fused features and unclassified object hypotheses. It qualifies the result using current capability; a negative classification or healthy sensor status does not prove SOTIF coverage. Requirements: TDS_ALG_001 through TDS_ALG_004, TDS_SAF_003 through TDS_SAF_005. "},"concept":"documentation","metamodel":"SysMLv2","namespace":"System_Model_Tiger_Detection"},
{"attributes":{"stable_path":"/documentation/Documentation@81e3475f-3443-4a0d-bbd3-95c673a76d61","sysml_id":"81e3475f-3443-4a0d-bbd3-95c673a76d61","element_id":"81e3475f-3443-4a0d-bbd3-95c673a76d61","sysml_type":"Documentation","owner_id":"60ed85a2-bbfa-4484-95ed-81c61fb18c37","owning_namespace_id":"60ed85a2-bbfa-4484-95ed-81c61fb18c37","owning_relationship_id":"23e01a1b-f07d-4e31-bf66-3f82684d837e","owning_membership_id":"23e01a1b-f07d-4e31-bf66-3f82684d837e","is_library_element":false,"is_implied_included":false,"body":"Monitored RGB + LWIR + lidar reference architecture. Sensor hardware\nsupplies measurements and available device diagnostics; channel-quality\nand blockage estimation are host software functions, not guaranteed\nembedded camera features. Fusion aligns data and produces unclassified\nhypotheses; ScanForTiger owns tiger classification. Requirement references identify the system contracts; SW requirements\ntrace to them through the RST satisfies attributes.\nThis is a behavioral/interface specification, not executable perception\nsoftware or validated safety evidence. Healthy status does not establish\nSOTIF performance for every pose, target size, or thermal contrast.\n"},"concept":"documentation","metamodel":"SysMLv2","namespace":"System_Model_Tiger_Detection"},
{"attributes":{"stable_path":"/documentation/Documentation@88e91c12-d1b2-415f-a520-323743bed3e6","sysml_id":"88e91c12-d1b2-415f-a520-323743bed3e6","element_id":"88e91c12-d1b2-415f-a520-323743bed3e6","sysml_type":"Documentation","owner_id":"7815083d-8b0a-4270-becd-0512ac7a3544","owning_namespace_id":"7815083d-8b0a-4270-becd-0512ac7a3544","owning_relationship_id":"22597e6b-451f-4342-9673-2fe1d4ce335a","owning_membership_id":"22597e6b-451f-4342-9673-2fe1d4ce335a","is_library_element":false,"is_implied_included":false,"body":"Aligns samples/features, qualifies each input and produces unclassified hypotheses. Invalid/unknown status is never treated as healthy. TDS_SEN_004. "},"concept":"documentation","metamodel":"SysMLv2","namespace":"System_Model_Tiger_Detection"},
{"attributes":{"stable_path":"/documentation/Documentation@899eb644-b51a-4ea5-a69d-17e4f446e2b3","sysml_id":"899eb644-b51a-4ea5-a69d-17e4f446e2b3","element_id":"899eb644-b51a-4ea5-a69d-17e4f446e2b3","sysml_type":"Documentation","owner_id":"fa3fd7ef-ecfc-4b47-a378-ab9106fe89eb","owning_namespace_id":"fa3fd7ef-ecfc-4b47-a378-ab9106fe89eb","owning_relationship_id":"ce4edd28-b6f4-43ff-8108-16f31791e191","owning_membership_id":"ce4edd28-b6f4-43ff-8108-16f31791e191","is_library_element":false,"is_implied_included":false,"body":"Waits for StartCommand, scans continuously while active, and stops\nscanning on StopCommand. Hosts the three sensor modalities and the\ncompute unit, which fuses them into a single detection result.\nRequirements: TDS_SAF_002, TDS_SEN_001, TDS_SEN_002, TDS_SEN_003,\nTDS_SEN_004.\n"},"concept":"documentation","metamodel":"SysMLv2","namespace":"System_Model_Tiger_Detection"},
{"attributes":{"stable_path":"/documentation/Documentation@8d01ddf2-2b52-431a-831c-5e2924c18b92","sysml_id":"8d01ddf2-2b52-431a-831c-5e2924c18b92","element_id":"8d01ddf2-2b52-431a-831c-5e2924c18b92","sysml_type":"Documentation","owner_id":"8ba7836f-ba43-4601-b0f0-61271cf9e166","owning_namespace_id":"8ba7836f-ba43-4601-b0f0-61271cf9e166","owning_relationship_id":"57c1a3f1-e3fa-416b-8b9a-4654e47aa3b9","owning_membership_id":"57c1a3f1-e3fa-416b-8b9a-4654e47aa3b9","is_library_element":false,"is_implied_included":false,"body":"Activates the audible alarm within the allowed level range and\ndisplays the detected tiger bearing and distance.\nRequirements: TDS_WRN_001, TDS_WRN_002, TDS_WRN_003, TDS_WRN_005.\n"},"concept":"documentation","metamodel":"SysMLv2","namespace":"System_Model_Tiger_Detection"},
{"attributes":{"stable_path":"/documentation/Documentation@8e0f4941-58fe-4dea-bb47-d3849e36227a","sysml_id":"8e0f4941-58fe-4dea-bb47-d3849e36227a","element_id":"8e0f4941-58fe-4dea-bb47-d3849e36227a","sysml_type":"Documentation","owner_id":"c754ce1e-a877-4f9e-ab39-929ddb8fb781","owning_namespace_id":"c754ce1e-a877-4f9e-ab39-929ddb8fb781","owning_relationship_id":"fc4a020a-c7bf-4f7c-9c0a-57a0cdf8bec0","owning_membership_id":"fc4a020a-c7bf-4f7c-9c0a-57a0cdf8bec0","is_library_element":false,"is_implied_included":false,"body":"LWIR calibration, freshness, blockage and contrast estimates. Thermal-specific thresholds require validation; no perfect blockage observability is assumed. TDS_SEN_005, TDS_ODD_006. "},"concept":"documentation","metamodel":"SysMLv2","namespace":"System_Model_Tiger_Detection"},
